s = s.replace("| Error-correcting sparse codes and a shared associative memory do not compress below one-hot tables at tested sizes | negative (H2) |", "| Error-correcting sparse codes and a shared associative memory do not compress below one-hot tables at tested sizes | negative (H2, I2, I3); H2's 'no exact Willshaw code at N >= 32' was an OR-readout artifact (corrected in I2) |\n| One shared fast-weight interpreter executes genuinely different programs exactly | supported (I3), but with no shared-capacity gain: fast memory, MACs and worst-case robustness scale linearly or worse with P (I3-I5) |\n| Perturbation targets (slow / fast / joint / fresh / activation) are different failure mechanisms | supported (I4): joint < either alone; slow-weight noise present at write time is absorbed, drift after writing is not |")
